      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Fermoyle Manor is an exclusive development of just eleven detached, contemporary homes, each crafted to the highest modern standards to deliver luxurious living in a private cul-de-sac setting. Perfectly located beside the heart of one of the region’s most picturesque and progressive villages, Fermoyle Manor combines superior design with an unrivalled lifestyle opportunity.\r\n\r\nThe development offers a choice of four distinct house types, ranging in size from 160m² (1,720 sq. ft.) to 226m² (2,437 sq. ft.). Each property features bright, spacious interiors designed for modern family life, complemented by generous private gardens to the front and rear, along with ample parking.\r\n\r\nPurchasing a home at Fermoyle Manor means more than acquiring a beautiful residence — it is an investment in an exceptional lifestyle. Residents will enjoy the peace and privacy of a tranquil setting, while remaining within easy reach of every amenity.\r\n\r\nLocation – The Best of Both Worlds\r\n\r\nKilanerin is a vibrant, thriving village just five minutes from Exit 22 of the M11, north of Gorey town, and a 45-minute drive from South Dublin. Over recent years, the village has developed an impressive range of facilities far beyond those typically found in villages of its size, including:\r\n\r\n•\tA state-of-the-art Leisure Centre with gym, sports hall, café, hairdressers, beauty salon, and office pods\r\n•\t7km of woodland walks through Curragh and Kilanerin Woods\r\n•\tLocal primary school, with school transport to Gorey’s second-level schools\r\n•\tSupermarket open 7 days, traditional village pub, and fully floodlit G.A.A. grounds with perimeter walking track\r\n•\tNearby Wexford Lavender Farm, accessible from Curragh Wood trails\r\n•\tExcellent country pursuits, from equestrian facilities to game shooting\r\n\r\nCroghan Mountain for trekking and hillwalking, offering panoramic views over the Irish Sea and even the mountains of Snowdonia on clear days\r\n\r\nA choice of stunning sandy beaches less than 10 minutes away, including Kilgorman, Clone, Saleen, and Ballymoney\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nNearby Gorey:\r\n\r\nThe bustling town of Gorey is just 7 minutes from Kilanerin. Known for its award-winning restaurants, lively pubs, and boutique shopping on Esmonde Street, Gorey also offers every modern convenience including major supermarkets, banks, schools, cultural organisations, and sports clubs.\r\n\r\nEducation: 3 modern secondary schools and 5 primary schools\r\n\r\nTransport:\r\n\r\n•\t24-hour bus service to Dublin City and Airport\r\n\r\n•\tUp to 34 daily services (Wexford Bus and Bus Éireann combined)\r\n\r\n•\tExcellent rail connections, including a Dublin commuter service\r\n\r\nRosslare Europort just 40 minutes away, with ferry services to the UK, France, and Spain"
      },
